ere judged items have them, and say so where none exists, as rule 7 does. Any new example from the pool must stay out of gold and dev.\n2. **Where rules 6 and 9 meet,** list the signals:\n   - Printed as fact: a dateline, an attributed source, or a named witness.\n   - A tale: a literary title, a narrator's framing, extended dialogue, or a moral.\n   - Where they conflict, the text's own framing decides, and the note says so.\n3. **Rule 16:** where several merged items are reports, the fields come from the item that holds the lexicon's match, else the first.\n4. **`place_type`:** the schema's values, `inn_or_hotel` and the rest.\n\n**Notes for later steps** (put them in the plan's 2C section now):\n- **2C.4:** when you draw the training data, re-check each drawn item against gold and dev with a stricter text rule, 0.05 of the shorter's runs and at least 4 runs. The 0.10/5 rule sits just under the lowest one-story pair (0.105, 6 runs), and a false flag on a training draw costs nothing.\n- **Step 7:** the pooled recall screen above.\n\n**2C.2: the labels.** Persona: ML specialist, as labeller. No model output of any kind may touch gold or dev until the labels are frozen: not the teacher, not base 4B, not Backboard.\n1. Commit POLICY v2 first.\n2. **Label all 300 gold and 150 dev yourself.**\n   - Read the crop wherever the OCR is unclear.\n   - Every label passes the page's `checked()`, quotes and choices included.\n   - Record each article's E-slices.\n3. **A blind second pass:** reading agents label every gold article again, and a seeded 20% of dev.\n   - They see only the text, its crop on request, and POLICY: no first labels, strata or weights.\n   - Report agreement before adjudication, each with an interval: raw agreement and Cohen's kappa on kind, agreement on report or not, and agreement per field on articles both call reports.\n   - Adjudicate every disagreement under POLICY, and keep both labels and the ruling.\n4. **Freeze:** commit labels.jsonl and dev_labels.jsonl with their sha256s, before any model output exists.\n5. **Measure on gold:**\n   - reports found per stratum and in all, against the 35.3 expected\n   - the weighted report rate\n   - the story-place rule, scored against the labelled `place_state`\n- Commit labels in batches as you go, so a usage limit costs nothing.\n\n**Gate**\n- 450 labels, all passing `checked()`.\n- The second pass's agreement, with intervals.\n- Every disagreement adjudicated.\n- The label hashes committed before any model output.\n- The story-place rule measured.\n- Decision 38 written.\n- Tests and lint pass, and the push is checked with `ls-remote`.\n- Report as before. The first line is `2C.2: GATE PASSED` or `2C.2: BLOCKED — <reason>`.","hostInjected":true},"promptSource":"system","queueSkipSlashCommands":true,"turnOrigin":"peer","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":0,"turnIndex":45},"queueSkipAttachments":true,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
