3\tstreet :,Dd CASTOR avenue to extln\n574\tguiyl. fines which had been caused\n575\tFy a fire caused by a defective ilue.\n576\tTic FIRE was soon extinguisheG\n577\t\n578\t\n579\tl'ha first Q ia series OF tie fires\n580\twhich occurred within few haltrs\n581\twas q fir. from an overheated Kinney\n582\tat the home Of George Graham on\n583\tMarket street This, fire occurred at\n584\t1870 Sunday morning and the East\n585\tSide department responded to tie call\n586\tand put cut the flames before they\n587\thad caused much damage.\n588\t\n589\t=== 106_1909-07-27_pna_sn84026749_100492465_1909072701_0292.json\n590\tThe Washington times. [volume] (Washington [D.C.]) 1902-1939 · 1909-07-27\n591\tcrops: None\n592\theadline: PALMISTS.\n593\t\n594\tSPIRITUALISM.\n595\t---\n596\tNINE. CORNISH, GIFTED MEDIUM reads\n597\tyour life correctly; gives names, facts daily\n598\tand Sunday. 601 Sd ST ~ E. cor. +, near\n599\tUnion Station. ladies' only. jyl-u\n600\t\n601\t=== 4_1879-06-23_pna_sn86053573_0021110238A_1879062301_0606.json\n602\tNational Republican. (Washington City (D.C.)) 1872-1888 · 1879-06-23\n603\tcrops: None\n604\theadline: HOUSE REpR Els ryTa 7rYEs.\n605\t---\n606\t\n607\t\n608\t\n609\tMr.. COBB, rising to question of personal priv\n610\tiege, sent to the Clerks desk and had read an OK\n611\ttract from the indianapolis journal of the 18th\n612\tinst, charging him with having repeated thread.\n613\tbare lie about Massachusetts, regiment interfering\n614\twith voters in indianapolis in October, 1864. lie\n615\talso had read extracts from other papers and letters\n616\treceived by him in corroboration Of the statement\n617\twhich he had made in his speech, and again re.\n618\titerated the charge that the election referred to had\n619\tbeen nterfered with by the Massachusetts, regl\n620\tment.\n621\t\n622\t\n623\tMr.. WARNER, who had been stationed at Indian.\n624\tnpols in October 1861, stated that It had officially\n625\tcome TO his knowledge there had been Interference