ward the door,\n1311\twhen, to our establishment, the sleeping\n1312\tfigure rose, or rather glided after him,\n1313\tout of the door, into the hall, down the\n1314\tstairs. and as he opened the front door\n1315\tStolberg called to Mrs. Cameron, who\n1316\tstood with me at the head of the stairs\n1317\twatching the results of this wonderful\n1318\tinfluence:\n1319\t\n1320\t\n1321\t\"You see, madame, she would follow\n1322\tme anywhere\" and, as though to prove\n1323\tit. she passed out of the door, which\n1324\tStolberg shut, and. TO my horror, heard\n1325\thim lock it after him.\n1326\t\n1327\t\n1328\tfew down the two flights of stairs\n1329\tinto the basement, my brain turning\n1330\tmad, it seemed TO me, and reached the\n1331\tsidewalk by the lower door just in time\n1332\tTO see carriage turning at full speed\n1333\tthe next corner.\n1334\t\n1335\t\n1336\tReturning to Mrs. Cameron | found\n1337\ther in a swoon, cut of which, as she\n1338\tawakened to sensibility, she passed into\n1339\tcommissions and at midnight was corpse.\n1340\tMeanwhile the police had been Informed,\n1341\tmessages sent in all directions, but OF\n1342\tStolberg or his unhappy victim / have\n1343\tnever heard since.-Bufalo News.\n1344\t\n1345\t=== 7_1866-06-26_pna_sn85025007_00415663596_1866062601_0202.json\n1346\tAlexandria gazette. [volume] (Alexandria, D.C.) 1834-1974 · 1866-06-26\n1347\tcrops: cached\n1348\theadline: \n1349\t---\n1350\tGORGE E. WHITE,\n1351\t\" Liberty Hall,\n1352\t\n1353\t\n1354\tSO and 81, Cameron street,\n1355\tInvites attention to his very extensive and\n1356\tchoice stock of\n1357\t\n1358\t\n1359\tGROCER les,\n1360\tembracing Teas, Cotfees, Sugars, Spices, Hams\n1361\tBacon. Flour Candles Soap, Molasses, Butter,\n1362\tCheese, Canned Meats and Fruits, Jellies, Far-\n1363\tna Corn Starch, and great variety Of articles,\n1364\tusually found in q grocery store.\n1365\t\n1366\t\n1367\tBRUCES\n1368\t\n1369\t\n1370\tCONCENTRATED FERTILIZER.\n1371\t\n1372\t\n1373\tSWAN ISL