{"parentUuid":"58ec75e2-cdbf-44e7-9fcf-a2098c07f5d9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"775e54ef-6487-4f79-8598-643421b87718","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0184jdbJx9Q7iBoyufMFCkrf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== 12_1848-05-06_p1_sn83016957_00200292443_1848050601_0502.json\n2\tBoon&#39;s Lick times. [volume] (Fayette, Mo.) 1840-1848 · 1848-05-06\n3\tcrops: cached\n4\theadline: Vol. D.\n5\t\n6\tTO THE EVENING ZEPHYR.\n7\t\n8\tBY MISS ALICE CAREY.\n9\t---\n10\t| sit where the wild bee i, humming,\n11\tAnd listen in vain for thy song;\n12\tI've waited before for thy coming,\n13\tBut never, oh never so long\n14\tHow Oft with the blue sky above us.\n15\t\n16\t\n17\tAnd waves breaking light on the shore,\n18\tThou, knowing they would not reprove us,\n19\tHast kissed me thousand times Ger\n20\tSo sweet were thy dewy embraces,\n21\t\n22\t\n23\tThy falsity who could believe\n24\tSome phantom thy fondness effaces-\n25\t\n26\t\n27\tThou could'st not have aimed to deceived\n28\tThou toldest thy love for me never,\n29\t\n30\t\n31\tBut all the brigh: stars in the skies,\n32\tthough striving TO do so forever,\n33\t\n34\t\n35\tCould scarcely have numbered thy signs.\n36\tAlone in the gathering shadows\n37\t\n38\t\n39\tStill waiting sweet Zephyr, for the.\n40\tlook for the waves OF the meadows.\n41\t\n42\t\n43\tAnd dimples to blot the blue sea.\n44\tThe blossoms tina. waited TO greet thee\n45\t\n46\t\n47\tWith the heat Of the noontide oppres,,\n48\tNow futter SO lightly to meet thee,\n49\t\n50\t\n51\tThou'r. coming. know, from the West.\n52\tAlas! if thou fndest me pouting,\n53\t\n54\t\n55\tIT'S only my love that alarms\n56\tForgive, then, pray thee, my doubling,\n57\t\n58\t\n59\tAnd take me once more to thy arms!\n60\t\n61\t=== 20_1883-01-06_p1_sn83016348_00415624578_1883010601_0367.json\n62\tThe Cecil Whig. · 1883-01-06\n63\tcrops: cached\n64\theadline: MATERIAL ApPARITlONS.\n65\t---\n66\tMhlEKlAL ApPARlTlONS\n67\t\n68\t\n69\tEnvelope