27\t\n428\t\n429\tFollow, follow,\n430\t\n431\t\n432\tWe will follow Roosevelt,\n433\t\n434\t\n435\tAnywhere he leads US,\n436\t\n437\t\n438\tWe will follow on.\n439\t\n440\t\n441\tAll of which being chanted to the\n442\travishing air Of that stirring ditty,\n443\tentitled We don't know where we're\n444\tgoing, but we're on the way brought\n445\tthe multitude into such a state of\n446\tblind and benighted ldolatry that au-\n447\tthentic information to the effect that\n448\tthe colonel had just waylaid per-\n449\tfectly respectable minister of the gos-\n450\tpei and robbed him of his last months\n451\tdonations would have brought forth\n452\tenthusiastic cheers for the colonel\n453\tand vote of stern condemnation for\n454\tthe man of God as the representative\n455\tof dangerous and Ubiquitous pluto\n456\tcracy.\n457\t\n458\t\n459\t\"In form two thousand delegates,\n460\tmore or less, gathered in the Col\n461\tiseum; in reality Mr.. Roosevelt met\n462\tin convention at Chicago, made a\n463\tconfession of faith, gave his hand to\n464\tthe colored brother from the North\n465\tand his foot to the colored brother\n466\tfrom the South, adopted a platform,\n467\tnominated himself and Brother john\n468\tson, and adjourned with the ease Of\n469\ta thoroughly trained thimblerigger\n470\tplying his vocation among the rural\n471\tvisitors to the midway plaisance.\n472\t\n473\t\n474\tTHE campaign upon which we are\n475\tabout, to enter presents issues OF\n476\tmore serious moment to the Ameri-\n477\tcan people than any they have con-\n478\tfronted since the grave questions\n479\twhich Immediately preceded and ac-\n480\tcompanicd the Civil War. The over\n481\tshadowing question then was whether\n482\tthe Union, under the Constitution,\n483\tcould be perpetu]ted; that which\n484\tconfronts us today is whether the\n485\tConstitution itself, and the govern\n486\tment which the Constitution estab-\n487\tlished, shall be preserved-a ques-\n488\tton of equal if not greater gravity,\n489\tsince it would be of little avail to\n490\thave preserved the Union from the\n491\tchaos of disintegration if the govern\n492\tment Of the Union is to be given over\n493\tto the chaos of disorganation.\n494\t\n495\t\n496\t1.-The party to which we belong, Mr..\n497\tVice President, stands in the supreme\n498\tcontest for the independence aud in\n499\ttegrity of the judicial tribunals of the\n500\tland, without which the guaranty of\n501\tlife, liberty, and property would be a\n502\tmeaningless platitude. 1t stands for\n503\tthe settled rule of impersonal gov\n504\teminent, as opposed to the shifty OPP\n505\tportunism of personal manipulation;\n506\tfor the liberty and order of general\n507\tlaw, as against the tyranny of spec\n508\tial edicts of changing men. 1t plants\n509\titself upon the impregnable ramparts\n510\tof the Constitution, and, solemnly\n511\tprotesting against any subverslon of\n512\tthe terms of that great compact by\n513\tthe arrogant and revolutionary pro-\n514\tces of amendment by misconstructlon.\n515\tappeals from the midsummer madness\n516\tof that portion of the people which\n517\tcan be fooled all the time to the sober\n518\tsecond thought of the great body of\n519\tthe American electorate who will\n520\trender judgment in November\n521\t\n522\t\n523\t\n524\t\n525\t=== 14_1907-09-05_p1_sn89067273_00200292662_1907090501_0301.json\n526\tMexico Missouri message. · 1907-09-05\n527\tcrops: cached\n528\theadline: stopped HseeIna rhInnn..\n529\t---\n530\tEnthusiastic Nature Lover Ito Re.\n531\tformed Tramp)-Ah, my friend, how\n532\twell you must know the face of ma.\n533\tture, and know It in all its moods.\n534\tHave you ever seen the sun sinking\n535\tin such a glare OF glory that 1t swal-\n536\tlows up the whole horizon with its\n537\tpassionate flre7 Have you seen the\n538\tmist gliding like specter down the\n539\tshrinking hillside. or the pale moon\n540\tstruggling to shake OF the grip Of the\n541\tragged storm cloud?\n542\t\n543\t\n544\tRef