ea Open Only\nz More Days, July 3-4,\n\n\nThis Season\n---\nPISGAH FOREST, June 2S.-\nEspecially Sherwood Cooperative\narea of Pisgah National forest\nwill be opened to fishermen on\nJuly 8 and 4, for its final public\nseason.\n\n\nOF the 26O fishermen who en-\ntered this area on May 7th and\n9Th, 1O7 caught their limit OF\nbrook trout, and the average\ncatch per man per day was 7.48\nfish of legal size. The Sherwood\narea is regarded. by the forestry\ndepartment as among the better\nfishing grounds Of the entire Sec\nton to be opened this season.\n\n\nAll streams in the forest have\nbeen fished this season, with Da-\nwilson River area providing an\naverage of 5.21 fish per n1an-day\nfor all entries. Largest fish aver\nage caught was in the North Mills\nRiver area, where the average was\nover six ounces per fish.\n\n\nForty three fishermen who\nchecked out of the North Mills\nRiver area during the weekend\nJust closed had an average OF\nover q pound of fish per man,\nwith one catch of a l9 IL inch\nrainbow reported.\n\n\nCoke Gambler of Gambler caught\nseven fish that had q total weight\nof five pounds. One Of Mr.. Can\ndler's beauties tipped the scales\nat three pounds, two and one-halt\nounces. j. C.. Courtney, also OF\nGambler, caught just two fish dur\ning his haunt, but his specimens\nweighed two pounds, one Of them\n15-inch rainbow.\n\n\nL. l. Barrett Of Asheville had\na 13-inch rainbow that weighed\none pound, FIVE ounces: DR.. G. N,\nCONTINUED on page four)\n\n=== 68_1856-07-30_p1_sn82015753_00212475385_1856073001_0834.json\nNew Orleans daily crescent. [volume] ([New Orleans, La.]) 1851-1866 · 1856-07-30\ncrops: cached\nheadline: p,YT,TssaaT,T T,rs,;AsrERs.\n---\ni B d 98-4~\n\n\nAmong Tie more important elements that have\ncontributed to the growth and prosperity q tns\ncountry rna properly Do classed railroads The vast\nextent Of territory, the varied interests and me ever\nactive spirit Of our people, have rendered neees-\nsary that speedy methods Of comm