edge.\nIL IS the patron OF agriculture, and nurse OF\nthe arts. II incites TO enterprise, and re-\ncompsnses industry. Ii associates the vari\n~txx, IL. L.. r\nthe regions of the earth and approxi.nates\nthe poles. AS prof able servant OF The\ncommon veal, let commerce be fosiered and\nprotected; but let not the independence of\nAmerica be sacrificed in mercantile specu-\nlation /; let not her distinguished immuni\nties and ineStimable liberties be the booked\nand legered items in the account of foreign\ntrade.\n\n\nThe progressive Improvement of domes\nTIC manufactures is Cause OF present ga\ntulation and rejoicing. Numerous hills\nwritten with f1eeces; unnumoered values la\nDor with plenty the plains wave with lux\nuriant harves. $; the teeming earth disc. SEES\nher secret treasures; universal abundance\niHvites the artist and the arts. b, remuv\ning the necessity of resnrtng to foreign\nchimes for supplies of the conveniences If\nlite, domestic manufactures promote the\n\n\n\n\n\nstrengthen the bonds of UNION between\nthe confederate states. by establishing inter\nnal commerce and increasing their mutual\nreliance.\n\n\nWhile the tempest of war has desolaJ ed\nthe natiors while the whirlwind of destruc\nton has wasted the Kingdoms, and overturn\ned the thrones of Europe while the sword\nhas consumed the people. and a deluge OF\nblood has drenched their fields. and over\nflowed with polluted streams our native\nskies have continued serene and fair Peace\nhas inhabited our borders, and security\ndwelt in our towns. Our civil privileges\nwhich were achieved by valor. have been\npreserved by wisdom. Our comforts which\nwere gained by enterprise, have been IN\ncreased by industry. Our institutions which\nwere founded by hberali y. have been fos\ntered by munihcence. The principles Of our\nconstitution of government rsmain uncaang\ned !; and so long as they shall endure, and\nthe integrity OF the federal union sh al CONT\nnue. unimpaired, Americans may rejoice in\nthe freedom, sovereignty & independence Of\nthe u 5. They shall endure forever. BY\nour brave fathers memories, by the awful\nshades of revolutionary martyrs, swear,\nthey shall endure forever,-f for, . though\nIndividuals may perish, truth is eternal.\nThe rude blasts or tyranny may blow from\nevery quarter, out freedom is marcy plant,\nthat viii survive the tempest, and strike\nan everlasting root in the most unfavorable\nsoil''\n\n\nColumbia, favorite of heaven. and hope OF\nthe world Rejoice Nature and Art unite\nto adorn thee! Wealth is thy handmade\nand wisdom and honor attend thy steps\nThe eagle will SOAR to the stars, and build her\neyry, where danger cannot climb. Nations\nwill seek shelter under the covert of her\nwings. The corners of the earth will bound\nthy power, and the confines of eternity limit\nthy glory\n","numLines":1407,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1407}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"58ec75e2-cdbf-44e7-9fcf-a2098c07f5d9","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"other"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/hotragn/Documents/Claude Code/HacktoberFest/week4/Paperghosts","sessionId":"1f5be3b0-ab69-4299-a8b5-d7494c65687b","version":"2.1.309","gitBranch":"phase-2c-reader","slug":"sunny-popping-comet"}
